  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#e-mail-state-(type=email)\r\n\r\n> /^\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\.\\!\\#$%&amp;'\\*\\+\\\\/=​?^\\_\\`\\{\\|\\}\\~\\-\\]\\+@​\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\]\\(?:​\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\-\\]\\{0,61\\}\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\]\\)?\\(?:​\\\\\\.\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\]\\(?:​\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\-\\]\\{0,61\\}\\[a\\-zA\\-Z0\\-9\\]\\)?\\)\\*$/\r\n\r\nShould this use {0,63} instead of {0,61}? given that https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#valid-e-mail-address says:\r\nlabel         = let-dig [ [ ldh-str ] let-dig ]  ; limited to a length of 63 characters by RFC 1034 section 3.5",
